WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.520
The Star Wars prequel trilogy gave fans of
the popular sci-fi franchise many things:

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.920
a look at Anakin Skywalker growing up and
an explanation as to how he became a Sith

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.520
Lord; a peek behind the curtain at the politics
fueling the Empire; a huge pet peeve in the

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.970
form of Jar-Jar Binks; and even a young Boba
Fett, the notorious bounty hunter from the

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.860
original trilogy.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.839
Boba Fett made his first appearance — chronologically
speaking, anyway — in Star Wars: Attack

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.960
of the Clones, the second installment in the
prequel trilogy.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.040
He also appeared as a youngster on the animated
series Star Wars: The Clone Wars, which gave

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.230
us the story of how Boba Fett began on the
path to becoming the galaxy's fiercest, and

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.920
most fearsome, bounty hunter.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.140
"You may take Captain Solo to Jabba the Hutt
after I have Skywalker."

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.120
"He's no good to me dead."

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.060
At the time of Attack of the Clones, the character
was only 10 years old and living on the planet

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.340
Kamino with his "father," bounty hunter Jango
Fett, of whom he was actually a clone.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.060
Child actor Daniel Logan portrayed young Boba
Fett on the big screen, but what happened

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.560
to him?

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.380
What has the kid who played the most famous
bounty hunter in the Star Wars universe been

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.840
up to in the years since he came back down
to Earth?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.440
For starters, the Star Wars prequels didn't
put Logan off from acting like they did with

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.880
young Anakin Skywalker actor Jake Lloyd.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.320
Rest assured that the 32-year-old New Zealander
is still in the biz to this day.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.940
After appearing in Attack of the Clones in
2002, Logan made a number of more low-key

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.000
appearances in films and on television.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.640
In 2003, he lent his voice to the animated
series TakaPu: A Gannet In The South Seas

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.370
and the feature film The Legend of Johnny
Lingo.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:37.170
He was even the voice behind the animated
incarnation of Boba Fett for five episodes

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.590
of The Clone Wars, which ran for five seasons
on Cartoon Network beginning in 2008.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.440
A sixth was produced for Netflix, and a seventh
will be fielded next year on Disney+.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.000
More recently, Logan has held roles in Sharknado
4: The 4th Awakens, playing a character named

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
— wait for it — Captain Fett.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.100
He also appeared The Griddle House, and Underdogs
Rising.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.280
He's set to appear in the theatrical feature
The Time War and the TV movie The Oath: Outbreak,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.980
both of which are currently in post-production.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.460
When the Star Wars sequel trilogy was announced,
there was also talk of a Boba Fett spin-off

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.750
film and at that time, photos surfaced of
Logan being kitted out in an adult Boba Fett

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:14.240
costume.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.040
The actor is active on social media, with
plenty of photos on Instagram to show he still

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:23.870
has young Boba's cheeky side grin, and he's
also shared a number of images of himself

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.880
trying on a full costume or bits and pieces
thereof.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.940
Of course, there's no doubt it was a costume
he commissioned for himself, as there's no

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.170
way a company like Disney would stand for
him sharing photos of an official costume

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.560
for a film before the studio had released
its own photos and trailers.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.470
Nothing was ever confirmed with regards to
a possible role for Logan in the Boba Fett

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:47.260
film, but it certainly wouldn't have been
outside the realm of possibility for him to

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.280
make a return to the Star Wars universe.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.960
It's quite clear that the actor would have
been more than happy to make a big comeback

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.440
in the franchise had the chance arisen; unfortunately,
the film was cancelled late in 2018, after

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.640
Solo: A Star Wars Story underperformed at
the box office.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.900
Logan still makes as many public appearances
as he can with other Star Wars franchise stars.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.870
He attends Comic Cons around the world, where
he poses for photos with fans and thanks them

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.100
for the continued support.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.840
Although he certainly isn't among Hollywood's
A-list after the promising early start to

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.050
his career, Logan is still in the industry
and reliving his Boba days as often as he

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:20.540
can.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:25.680
The actor is also married and has an adorable
little clone of his own, his young son Brad,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.740
who might just follow in his father's footsteps.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.480
Sound like someone else we know?

